{
  "id": "go-build-undefined",
  "title": "Go build breaks after ParseConfig was renamed to LoadConfig",
  "description": "PR #73 adds INVENTORY_* environment overrides to internal/config and renames config.ParseConfig to config.LoadConfig. It updates the tests and cmd/migrate/main.go, but cmd/server/main.go (not touched by the PR) still calls config.ParseConfig. `go build -v ./...` prints ~250 package names from a cold build (the setup-go cache restore failed with a 503, an unrelated warning) and ends with `cmd/server/main.go:26:21: undefined: config.ParseConfig`; Vet and Test are skipped. The lint job fails as a cascade with the same compile error reported by golangci-lint as (typecheck), and docker is skipped because it needs both. Correct answer: a code error introduced by the rename; update the remaining caller in cmd/server/main.go to config.LoadConfig (keeping a deprecated ParseConfig wrapper would also work). The cache 503 is noise, not the cause.",
